      "message": "build: speed up grunt by using ignore\n\nGrunt tasks takes files targets defined by pattern. It calls node-glob\nfor each pattern which does a full tree traversal then merge the lists\nand excludes the files matched by negate pattern.\n\ntyops has 9 patterns which causes a full tree traversal of 47486 files\nwhen node_modules and vendor are populated it then rejects most of them\nto end up with a set of 578 files.\n\nLooking at https://gruntjs.com/configuring-tasks#files , the built-in\n`src` passes options to the underlying node-glob and\nhttps://github.com/isaacs/minimatch. node-glob supports ignoring files\nentirely, which make it dramatically faster by reducing the number of\npatterns (and thus calls to glob) and early discarding a whole directory\ntraversal (eg .git/**).\n\nAdd common patterns (.git, node_modules...) in a shared variable so they\ncan be applied to tops, eslint and stylelint.\n\nReplace `**/docs/**` by `docs/**`.\n\nResults when running `./node_modules/.bin/grunt`:\n\n\u003d\u003d tyops \u003d\u003d\n\n578 files in 1m5.4s\n578 files in 1.9s\n\n\u003d\u003d eslint \u003d\u003d\n\n9s to 6s\n\nThe task is given `src: \u0027.\u0027` which still causes Grunt to do a full path\ntraversal, eslint however its own ignore list in .eslintignore and thus\nthe benefit is less noticeable.\n\n\u003d\u003d stylelint \u003d\u003d\n\n94 files in 14.8s\n94 files in 5.9s\n\nTotal time went from near 2 minutes down to 15s!\n\nBug: T438811\nChange-Id: I8f802291039467f1d8e1af8c2ec2e3a5c346868d\n"
    },
