      "message": "TemplateDataCache: Restore behaviour lost in the ApiResponseCache move\n\nThis is a follow-up to Ic8076ab3, which replaced MWTransclusionModel\u0027s\nAPI calls and cache with a ve.init.mw.ApiReponseCache.\n\n* The API call lose `formatversion\u003d2`. The old code used\n  Target\u0027s getContentApi, which sets it. (This is the root cause of\n  several of the following issues.)\n* The transclusion dialog no longer reports that a template does not\n  exist. VE does not record missing templates, because formatversion\u003d1\u0027s\n  missing flag is an empty string, which is falsy.\n* The \"no TemplateData\" notice does not show, because isDocumented()\n  gives the wrong answer. The notemplatedata flag is also an empty\n  string, and so undocumented templates report as documented.\n* TemplateDiscovery doesn\u0027t show the favorite button on individual\n  template pages. The page id is missing from the cached response.\n* Two redirects to one template conflict. The base class stops at the\n  first mapped title. The second redirect gets no data.\n\nMinor:\n* One bad title loses the whole fetch. Promise.all rejects, so no part\n  reaches the change queue and the dialog waits forever.\n* reset() clears a property that no longer exists. Nothing declares or\n  reads templateDataApiRequests.\n* The commit deprecated a private method. markRequestAsDone has no\n  external callers.\n\nBug: T162694\nChange-Id: I803a13ec607a489a7f4aed792b63e5667ec025b5\n"
    },
