      "message": "DuplicateLinkEditCheck: fix merging links in complex annotations\n\nThis change spreads annotations covering both ends of the adjacent link\nranges across the intervening space. If this cannot be done, we just\ndon\u0027t show the suggestion.\n\nSimplified real example: `\u0027\u0027A, [[B]]\u0027\u0027 [[B|\u0027\u0027B2\u0027\u0027]]\u0027\u0027, \u0027\u0027C` would offer a\nmerge, but not do anything.\n\nThe merge *did* clear the range, and then set a single link annotation\nover the whole range. However, because of the incompletely-covering\nitalics, when we reserialized the document to save we\u0027d have to close\nout the `\u003ci\u003e` and the `\u003ca\u003e`... and then `trimWhitespace` would mean\nwe\u0027d remove that space between words from the second opening `\u003ca\u003e`.\nThus we\u0027d reproduce the original duplicate-linked version of the\nwikitext.\n\nThis would result in `\u0027\u0027A, [[B|B B2]], \u0027\u0027C` for the above example.\n\nBug: T437749\nChange-Id: I9a61b515e05ac326bfef045ab4b01eda7a655c48\n"
    },
